# Accepted vulnerability exceptions — single source of truth.
#
# Consumed by:
#   - Trivy (natively, in CI and scripts/security/scan-trivy.sh)
#   - scripts/security/scan-dependencies.sh (parses CVE-*/GHSA-* lines to
#     filter bun audit output)
#
# For each accepted finding, list the CVE id (matched by Trivy) AND the GHSA
# id (matched against bun audit output) when both exist, each on its own
# line, with a justification comment. Remove entries as soon as a fix is
# applied.
#
# picomatch ReDoS through single-branch repeated extglobs (<=4.0.7). 4.0.7 is the
# latest release and no patched version exists yet, so a lockfile refresh cannot
# fix it. picomatch is only reached through build and test tooling (vite, vitest,
# svelte-check, eslint, paraglide's unplugin); the running server never matches
# user-supplied glob patterns. Remove both lines once a patched picomatch ships.
CVE-2026-112366
GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf
